course: dictionary
lesson: 1050
title: Context clues from a bowl of soup
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Context means the words around a new word, and they often give clues. «"Borscht", the beetroot soup closely linked to Ukraine» tells you borscht is a soup, and that it is made from beetroot.
explain: Look for more clues. Borscht is usually red, sour and eaten in Ukraine and other Eastern European countries. Now try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. "The beetroot soup closely linked to Ukraine" still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Borscht is a noun, and it is uncountable. You say a bowl of borscht, not three borschts, just as you say a glass of milk.
fact: Borscht is a sour soup, usually red from beetroot.
fact: It is often made with cabbage, potatoes, meat and beans, and served with sour cream and dill.
fact: Borscht reached English through Yiddish from the Slavic word «борщ».
fact: In 2022, UNESCO listed Ukrainian borscht cooking as heritage needing urgent protection.
fact: Families each have their own recipe, and there is also green borscht made with sorrel.
exercise: «Borscht, the beetroot soup closely linked to Ukraine, is a famous dish.» What is borscht? | *A sour soup, usually red from beetroot | A sweet cake with cream | A kind of dance from Ukraine | A type of bread baked in a tin
exercise: Borscht is often served with what? | *Sour cream and dill | Custard and sugar | Jam and toast | Ketchup and chips
exercise: The sentence links borscht closely to which country? | *Ukraine | Mexico | France | Japan
test: Borscht reached English through which language? | Latin | Ukrainian | English | *Yiddish
test: In 2022, what did UNESCO do with Ukrainian borscht cooking? | *Listed it as heritage needing urgent protection | Banned it | Moved it to another country | Gave it a prize for the best cook
exam: Tom reads «a bowl of hot borscht with sour cream» and does not know what borscht is. What should he do? | *Use the clues: hot, bowl and sour cream suggest a soup, then check his meaning fits the sentence | Give up because he cannot understand the text | Eat the sour cream and guess | Look for a word that rhymes with borscht
